#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084441 :tutorial/content "The **general standard equation** of a hyperbola centered at $(h, k)$ has two forms.\n\n- The equation for a horizontal hyperbola is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {(x - h)^2} {a^2} - \\dfrac {(y - k)^2} {b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\n![](images/86/86896528522f859d4809e922a52e03244fb5279248093dddf302d730e9a542e5.png)\n\n- The equation for a vertical hyperbola is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {(y - k)^2} {a^2} - \\dfrac {(x - h)^2} {b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b099f7c4bc8b68e55b17dada9038a934c7bad668e0f4de518c603b1ca58f45.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "d86d9561-74bd-5438-8125-87229308ffb8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3492 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
